From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Farid Zakaria <farid.m.zakaria@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:32:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386: report a read-modify-write fault as a write

A CPU reads a read-modify-write instruction's memory destination for
ownership, so a page fault there carries the W bit in its error code.
TCG loads the destination with a plain load first, and the fault it
raises says read. A guest that reports the error code, as Linux does
for a segfault, then says another thing than it does on hardware:
addl $1, 0x108(%rax) on a NULL pointer printed error 4 under TCG and
error 6 under KVM.

Unlocked ALU operations other than CMP, INC, DEC, NOT, NEG, the
shifts and rotates, XADD, CMPXCHG and BTS, BTR and BTC now check the
destination for a write before they load it. Locked forms use atomic
operations, which already do.
